WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Merry christmas, grandpa.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Oh, merry christmas to you, stevie.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Did you bring me any presents?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Now, why would i want to do that?

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
'Cause it's christmas.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Oh, i thought santa claus

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Brought the presents at christmas.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.608
You have been a good boy
this year, haven't you?

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:02.638
I have, i swear.

00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:04.978
Well, then, who
knows?Maybe he'll come.

00:00:40.608 --> 00:00:42.538
Santa!

00:00:51.008 --> 00:00:52.838
Reindeer.

00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:39.808
Santa?

00:01:57.308 --> 00:02:00.178
Um, my daughter and
i were in our beds.

00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:03.138
Mike was downstairs
decorating the tree.

00:02:03.178 --> 00:02:05.508
I heard a thump on the roof,

00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:07.778
And then i-I heard mike scream,

00:02:07.808 --> 00:02:10.078
And now i'm talking to the fbi.

00:02:10.108 --> 00:02:12.208
And you didn't see any of it?

00:02:12.238 --> 00:02:15.608
No, he was... he was just gone.

00:02:15.638 --> 00:02:17.678
The doors were locked?There
was no forced entry?

00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:18.678
That's right.

00:02:18.708 --> 00:02:20.208
Does anybody else
have a key?My parents.

00:02:20.238 --> 00:02:21.878
Where do they live?

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.338
Florida.

00:02:23.378 --> 00:02:25.638
Thanks for letting me have
a look around, mrs. Walsh.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.038
I think we, uh, got just
about everything we need.

00:02:28.078 --> 00:02:29.808
We're all set.

00:02:29.838 --> 00:02:31.308
We'll be in touch.

00:02:35.108 --> 00:02:36.938
Agents...

00:02:38.438 --> 00:02:41.038
T
- The police said my husband might have been kidnapped.

00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:42.408
Could be.

00:02:42.438 --> 00:02:45.178
Then why haven't
the kidnappers called

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:47.408
O- Or - Or
demanded a ransom?

00:02:47.438 --> 00:02:49.578
It's three days till christmas.

00:02:49.608 --> 00:02:52.208
What am i supposed
to tell our daughter?

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.138
We're very sorry.

00:03:02.308 --> 00:03:04.038
Find anything?

00:03:04.078 --> 00:03:06.978
Stockings, mistletoe... this.

00:03:07.008 --> 00:03:08.938
A tooth?Where was this?

00:03:08.978 --> 00:03:10.538
In the chimney.

00:03:10.578 --> 00:03:12.808
No way a man fits up a
chimney. It's too narrow.

00:03:12.838 --> 00:03:14.408
No way he fits up in one piece.

00:03:14.438 --> 00:03:16.538
All right, so, if dad
went up the chimney -

00:03:16.578 --> 00:03:18.738
We need to find out what
dragged him up there.

00:03:26.378 --> 00:03:28.638
So, was i right?

00:03:28.678 --> 00:03:31.208
Is it the serial-Killing
chimney sweep?

00:03:31.238 --> 00:03:32.378
Yep.

00:03:32.408 --> 00:03:34.978
It's, uh, it's
actually dick van dyke.

00:03:35.008 --> 00:03:35.908
Who?

00:03:35.938 --> 00:03:37.708
"Mary poppins. "Who's that?

00:03:37.738 --> 00:03:39.108
Oh, come on -Never mind.

00:03:39.138 --> 00:03:41.038
It turns out that walsh
is the second guy in town

00:03:41.078 --> 00:03:42.978
Grabbed out of his
house this month.

00:03:43.008 --> 00:03:44.208
Oh, yeah?Yeah.

00:03:44.238 --> 00:03:46.238
The other guy get dragged
up the chimney, too?

00:03:46.278 --> 00:03:49.478
Don't know. Witnesses said
they heard a thump on the roof.

00:03:49.508 --> 00:03:51.238
So, what the hell do you
think we're dealing with?

00:03:51.278 --> 00:03:53.538
Actually, i have an idea. Yeah?

00:03:53.578 --> 00:03:55.238
It's, uh, it's gonna sound crazy.

00:03:55.278 --> 00:03:57.638
What could you possibly
say that sounds crazy to me?

00:03:59.978 --> 00:04:01.408
Evil santa.

00:04:02.838 --> 00:04:04.308
Yeah, that's crazy.

00:04:04.338 --> 00:04:06.308
Yeah... i mean, i'm just saying

00:04:06.338 --> 00:04:09.838
That there's some version of
the anti-Claus in every culture.

00:04:09.878 --> 00:04:11.908
You got belsnickel,
krampus, black peter.

00:04:11.938 --> 00:04:14.638
Whatever you want to call
it, there's all sorts of lore.

00:04:14.678 --> 00:04:15.908
Saying what?

00:04:15.938 --> 00:04:18.008
Saying back in the day,
santa's brother went rogue,

00:04:18.038 --> 00:04:19.608
And now he shows up
around christmastime.

00:04:19.638 --> 00:04:21.608
Instead of bringing presents,
he punishes the wicked.

00:04:21.638 --> 00:04:23.008
By hauling their ass up chimneys?

00:04:23.038 --> 00:04:24.508
For starters, yeah.

00:04:24.538 --> 00:04:27.478
So, this is your theory,
huh? Santa's shady brother?

00:04:27.508 --> 00:04:30.438
Well, i'm just saying,
that's what the lore says.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:32.308
Santa doesn't have a
brother. There is no santa.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.678
Yeah, i know.

00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:34.938
You're the one who told
me that in the first place

00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:35.938
Remember?

00:04:41.478 --> 00:04:42.408
Yeah, you know
what?I could be wrong.

00:04:42.438 --> 00:04:44.778
I...

00:04:44.808 --> 00:04:46.138
...got to be wrong.

00:04:46.178 --> 00:04:47.778
Maybe, maybe not.

00:04:47.808 --> 00:04:49.708
What?

00:04:49.738 --> 00:04:52.638
I did a little digging
- Turns out both victims

00:04:52.678 --> 00:04:54.678
Visited the same place
before they got snatched.

00:04:54.708 --> 00:04:55.908
Where?

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:10.978
It does kind of lend credence
to the theory, don't it?

00:05:11.008 --> 00:05:13.078
Yeah, but anti-Claus?

00:05:13.108 --> 00:05:14.778
Couldn't be.

00:05:14.808 --> 00:05:16.308
It's a christmas miracle.

00:05:16.338 --> 00:05:18.808
Hey, speaking of, we
should have one this year.

00:05:18.838 --> 00:05:21.008
Have one what?A christmas.

00:05:21.038 --> 00:05:22.478
No, thanks.

00:05:22.508 --> 00:05:24.938
No, we'll get a tree,
a little boston market -

00:05:24.978 --> 00:05:26.678
Just like when we were little.

00:05:26.708 --> 00:05:29.408
Dean, those weren't exactly
hallmark memories for me.

00:05:29.438 --> 00:05:30.538
What are you talking about?

00:05:30.573 --> 00:05:31.638
We had some great christmases.

00:05:31.678 --> 00:05:33.178
Whose childhood are
you talking about?

00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:34.978
Oh, come on, sam.

00:05:35.008 --> 00:05:37.778
No, just... no.

00:05:39.408 --> 00:05:41.338
All right, grinch.

00:06:00.038 --> 00:06:02.578
What is that?

00:06:02.608 --> 00:06:04.238
A present for dad.

00:06:04.278 --> 00:06:06.178
Yeah, right.

00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:08.338
Where'd you get
the money -Steal it?

00:06:08.378 --> 00:06:10.838
No. Uncle bobby gave
it to me to give to him.

00:06:10.878 --> 00:06:12.408
Said it was real special.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.678
What is it?

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:15.038
A pony.

00:06:15.078 --> 00:06:17.378
Very funny.

00:06:22.308 --> 00:06:24.038
Dad's gonna be here, right?

00:06:24.078 --> 00:06:25.478
He'll be here.

00:06:25.508 --> 00:06:27.208
It's christmas.

00:06:27.238 --> 00:06:28.738
He knows.

00:06:28.778 --> 00:06:30.738
And he'll be here -Promise.

00:06:30.778 --> 00:06:32.078
Where is he, anyway?

00:06:32.108 --> 00:06:33.138
On business.

00:06:33.178 --> 00:06:34.438
What kind of business?

00:06:34.478 --> 00:06:36.138
You know that.

00:06:36.178 --> 00:06:37.808
He sells stuff.

00:06:37.838 --> 00:06:40.308
What kind of stuff?Stuff.

00:06:40.338 --> 00:06:42.108
Nobody ever tells me anything.

00:06:42.138 --> 00:06:44.108
Then quit asking.

00:06:52.838 --> 00:06:54.638
Is dad a spy?

00:06:54.678 --> 00:06:56.738
Mm-Hmm. He's james bond.

00:06:56.778 --> 00:06:58.838
Why do we move around so much?

00:06:58.878 --> 00:07:01.808
'Cause everywhere we go,
they get sick of your face.

00:07:04.908 --> 00:07:07.308
I'm old enough, dean.
You can tell me the truth.

00:07:07.338 --> 00:07:11.008
You don't want to know
the truth. Believe me.

00:07:11.038 --> 00:07:13.938
Is that why we never
talk about... mom?

00:07:13.978 --> 00:07:15.108
Shut up!

00:07:15.138 --> 00:07:18.078
<i>Don't you ever talk about mom
- Ever!</i>

00:07:21.408 --> 00:07:23.408
Wait. Where are you going?

00:07:23.438 --> 00:07:25.408
Out.

00:07:33.408 --> 00:07:36.208
You'd think with the 10 bucks
it costs to get into this place,

00:07:36.238 --> 00:07:38.578
Santa could scrounge
up a little snow.

00:07:40.738 --> 00:07:42.508
What?

00:07:42.538 --> 00:07:46.208
Nothing. What are we
looking for, again?

00:07:48.338 --> 00:07:51.238
Lore says that the anti-Claus

00:07:51.278 --> 00:07:54.578
Will walk with a limp
and smell like sweets.

00:07:54.608 --> 00:07:56.908
Great. So we're looking
for a pimp santa.

00:07:56.938 --> 00:07:58.278
Why the sweets?

00:07:58.308 --> 00:08:00.038
Think about it, dean.

00:08:00.078 --> 00:08:01.203
If you smell like candy

00:08:01.238 --> 00:08:03.938
The kids will come
closer, you know?

00:08:03.978 --> 00:08:05.778
That's creepy.

00:08:05.808 --> 00:08:07.238
How does this thing know

00:08:07.278 --> 00:08:09.678
Who's been naughty
and who's been nice?

00:08:09.708 --> 00:08:11.438
I don't know.

00:08:13.038 --> 00:08:16.139
So, ronny, come
sit on santa's knee.

00:08:16.178 --> 00:08:17.438
Ah, there you go.

00:08:17.478 --> 00:08:19.708
You been a good boy this year?Yeah

00:08:19.738 --> 00:08:22.208
Good.

00:08:22.238 --> 00:08:25.009
Santa's got a special gift for you

00:08:27.509 --> 00:08:28.978
Maybe we do

00:08:32.708 --> 00:08:34.678
Welcome to santa's court.

00:08:34.708 --> 00:08:36.208
Can i escort your child to santa?

00:08:36.238 --> 00:08:37.778
N
- No. No.

00:08:37.808 --> 00:08:39.608
Uh, but, actually,
my brother here -

00:08:39.639 --> 00:08:41.009
It's been a lifelong dream of his.

00:08:42.379 --> 00:08:46.238
Uh, sorry. No kids over... 12.

00:08:46.278 --> 00:08:48.879
No, he's just kidding. We
only came here to watch.

00:08:54.938 --> 00:08:58.238
I- I didn't mean that
we came here to w-Y

00:08:58.278 --> 00:09:00.838
Thanks a lot, dean.
Thanks for that.

00:09:02.278 --> 00:09:03.509
Check it out.

00:09:14.838 --> 00:09:16.308
Are you seeing this?

00:09:16.338 --> 00:09:18.408
A lot of people walk
with limps, right?

00:09:18.438 --> 00:09:20.978
Tell me you didn't smell
that. That was candy, man.

00:09:21.009 --> 00:09:23.278
That was ripple
- I think. Had to be.

00:09:25.379 --> 00:09:27.708
Maybe. We willing
to take that chance?

00:09:29.608 --> 00:09:33.208
What time is it?

00:09:33.238 --> 00:09:35.908
Same as the last time you asked.

00:09:35.938 --> 00:09:37.808
Here.

00:09:37.838 --> 00:09:39.438
Caffeinate.

00:09:47.509 --> 00:09:49.438
Wonderful.

00:09:52.708 --> 00:09:54.139
Hey, sam...

00:09:54.178 --> 00:09:56.978
Yeah?

00:09:57.009 --> 00:09:59.509
Why are you the boy
that hates christmas?

00:09:59.538 --> 00:10:02.438
Dean... i mean, i admit it -

00:10:02.478 --> 00:10:05.009
We had a few bumpy holidays
when we were kids. "Bumpy"?

00:10:05.038 --> 00:10:07.608
That was then. We'll
do it right this year.

00:10:07.639 --> 00:10:09.938
Look, dean, if you
want to have christmas

00:10:09.973 --> 00:10:11.538
Knock yourself out.

00:10:11.578 --> 00:10:13.238
Just don't involve me.

00:10:15.238 --> 00:10:16.778
Oh, yeah, that'd be great -

00:10:16.808 --> 00:10:19.108
Me and myself making
cranberry molds.

00:10:33.639 --> 00:10:35.278
What's up with saint nicotine?

00:10:47.938 --> 00:10:48.978
What?

00:10:49.009 --> 00:10:50.238
Nothing.

00:10:50.278 --> 00:10:52.578
It's just that,
uh... well, you know,

00:10:52.608 --> 00:10:54.838
Mr. Gung ho christmas might
have to blow away santa.

00:11:01.178 --> 00:11:04.338
What the hell are you doing here?

00:11:04.379 --> 00:11:06.879
I'm really not interested, okay?

00:11:13.738 --> 00:11:15.009
Jingle my bells...

00:11:15.038 --> 00:11:18.908
S
- Silent night

00:11:20.278 --> 00:11:22.509
Holy...

00:11:22.538 --> 00:11:25.408
...night... night

00:11:25.438 --> 00:11:28.379
* all is well * all is well

00:11:28.408 --> 00:11:31.509
* all is dry

00:11:31.538 --> 00:11:32.678
* bright

00:11:32.708 --> 00:11:35.838
* 'round and 'round

00:11:35.879 --> 00:11:38.938
* the table...

00:12:06.408 --> 00:12:09.038
Santa, you're early!

00:13:42.478 --> 00:13:43.978
So, that's how your son
described the attack?

00:13:44.778 --> 00:13:46.879
"Santa took daddy up the chimney"?

00:13:46.908 --> 00:13:48.808
That's what he says, yes.

00:13:48.838 --> 00:13:50.178
And where were you?

00:13:50.208 --> 00:13:51.408
I was asleep.

00:13:51.438 --> 00:13:53.678
And all of a sudden...

00:13:54.908 --> 00:13:56.908
...i was being dragged
out of bed, screaming.

00:13:56.938 --> 00:13:58.978
Did you see the attacker?

00:14:00.379 --> 00:14:03.108
It was dark, and he hit me.

00:14:03.139 --> 00:14:04.379
He knocked me out.

00:14:04.408 --> 00:14:06.938
I'm sorry. I know this is hard.

00:14:06.978 --> 00:14:10.078
Yeah... um, mrs. Caldwell,

00:14:10.108 --> 00:14:12.408
Where did you get that
wreath above the fireplace?

00:14:19.009 --> 00:14:20.838
Excuse me?

00:14:25.009 --> 00:14:27.408
Just curious, you know.

00:14:30.338 --> 00:14:31.509
Wreaths, huh?

00:14:31.538 --> 00:14:33.408
Sure you didn't want to
ask her about her shoes?

00:14:33.438 --> 00:14:35.308
I saw some nice
handbags in the foyer.

00:14:35.338 --> 00:14:37.608
We've seen that
wreath before, dean.

00:14:37.639 --> 00:14:38.678
Where?

00:14:38.708 --> 00:14:41.308
The walshes'.Yesterday.

00:14:41.338 --> 00:14:43.778
I know, i was just testing you.

00:14:47.379 --> 00:14:51.078
Yeah. All right. Well,
keep looking, would you?

00:14:51.108 --> 00:14:52.639
Thanks, bobby.

00:14:56.438 --> 00:14:58.108
What did bobby say?

00:14:58.139 --> 00:15:00.078
Uh, that we're morons.

00:15:00.108 --> 00:15:01.509
He also said

00:15:01.538 --> 00:15:04.178
That it was probably
meadowsweet in those wreaths.

00:15:04.208 --> 00:15:06.278
Wow! Amazing.

00:15:06.308 --> 00:15:08.108
What the hell is meadowsweet?

00:15:08.139 --> 00:15:09.509
It's pretty rare,

00:15:09.538 --> 00:15:11.478
And it's probably the most
powerful plant in pagan lore.

00:15:11.509 --> 00:15:13.639
Pagan lore? Yeah.

00:15:13.678 --> 00:15:16.338
See, they used meadowsweet
for human sacrifices.

00:15:16.379 --> 00:15:18.808
It was kind of like
a... chum for their gods.

00:15:18.838 --> 00:15:21.108
Gods were drawn to
it, and they'd stop by

00:15:21.139 --> 00:15:22.879
And snack on whatever
was the nearest human.

00:15:22.908 --> 00:15:25.009
Why would somebody be using
that for christmas wreaths?

00:15:25.038 --> 00:15:26.978
It's not as crazy
as it sounds, dean.

00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:29.708
I mean, pretty much every
christmas tradition is pagan.

00:15:29.738 --> 00:15:31.639
Christmas is jesus' birthday.

00:15:31.678 --> 00:15:34.108
No, jesus' birthday was
probably in the fall.

00:15:34.139 --> 00:15:36.478
It was actually the
winter solstice festival

00:15:36.509 --> 00:15:38.808
That was co-Opted by the
church and renamed "christmas. "

00:15:38.838 --> 00:15:41.009
But the yule log, the
tree, even santa's red suit

00:15:41.038 --> 00:15:42.639
That's all remnants
of pagan worship.

00:15:42.678 --> 00:15:44.108
How do you know that?

00:15:44.139 --> 00:15:45.578
What are you gonna tell me next?

00:15:45.608 --> 00:15:47.338
Easter bunny's jewish?

00:15:48.879 --> 00:15:51.408
So, you think we're
dealing with a pagan god?

00:15:51.438 --> 00:15:55.538
Yeah, probably hold nickar,
god of the winter solstice.

00:15:55.578 --> 00:15:58.708
And all these martha
stewart wannabes,

00:15:58.738 --> 00:16:00.509
Buying these fancy wreaths...

00:16:00.538 --> 00:16:03.278
It's pretty much like putting
a neon sign on your front door

00:16:03.308 --> 00:16:04.379
Saying, "come kill us. "

00:16:04.408 --> 00:16:05.978
Great.

00:16:07.438 --> 00:16:09.078
When you sacrifice to hold nickar,

00:16:09.108 --> 00:16:11.078
Guess what he gives you in return.

00:16:11.108 --> 00:16:12.478
Lap dances, hopefully.

00:16:12.509 --> 00:16:13.808
Mild weather.

00:16:16.408 --> 00:16:18.139
Like no snow in the
middle of december

00:16:18.178 --> 00:16:19.938
In the middle of
michigan. For instance.

00:16:19.978 --> 00:16:21.408
Do we know how to kill it yet?

00:16:21.438 --> 00:16:23.038
No, bobby's working
on that right now.

00:16:23.078 --> 00:16:25.379
We got to figure out where
they're selling those wreaths.

00:16:25.408 --> 00:16:27.978
You think they're
selling them on purpose?

00:16:28.009 --> 00:16:30.178
Feeding the victims to this thing?

00:16:31.678 --> 00:16:33.078
Let's find out.

00:16:41.809 --> 00:16:43.038
Help you boys?

00:16:43.079 --> 00:16:44.508
Uh, hope so.

00:16:44.538 --> 00:16:47.579
Uh, we were playing jenga with
the walshes the other night,

00:16:47.609 --> 00:16:50.478
And he hasn't shut up since
about this christmas wreath.

00:16:50.508 --> 00:16:52.478
I don't know. You tell him.

00:16:52.508 --> 00:16:54.339
Sure.

00:16:56.038 --> 00:16:57.579
It was yummy.

00:17:01.408 --> 00:17:04.038
I sell a lot of wreaths, guys.

00:17:04.079 --> 00:17:06.108
Right, right, but you see,

00:17:06.139 --> 00:17:08.079
This one would have
been really special.

00:17:08.108 --> 00:17:12.239
It had, uh, it had, uh, green
leaves, um, white buds on it.

00:17:12.278 --> 00:17:14.608
It might have been made
of, uh, meadowsweet?

00:17:14.639 --> 00:17:17.208
Well... aren't you a fussy one?

00:17:18.978 --> 00:17:20.938
He is.

00:17:20.978 --> 00:17:22.838
Anyway, i know the one
you're talking about.

00:17:22.878 --> 00:17:24.278
I'm all out.

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:26.608
Seems like this meadowsweet
stuff's rare and expensive.

00:17:26.639 --> 00:17:28.079
Why make wreaths out of it?

00:17:28.108 --> 00:17:29.778
Beats me. I didn't make them.

00:17:29.809 --> 00:17:30.978
Who did?

00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:32.338
Madge carrigan a local lady.

00:17:32.378 --> 00:17:35.139
Said the wreaths were so
special, she gave them for free.

00:17:35.179 --> 00:17:37.108
She didn't charge you? Nope.

00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:38.608
Did you sell them for free?

00:17:38.639 --> 00:17:39.838
Hell, no. It's christmas.

00:17:39.878 --> 00:17:41.679
People pay a buttload
for this crap.

00:17:41.708 --> 00:17:42.778
That's the spirit.

00:17:45.239 --> 00:17:48.878
How much do you think a
meadowsweet wreath would cost?

00:17:48.909 --> 00:17:50.809
A couple hundred dollars, at least.

00:17:50.838 --> 00:17:52.909
This lady's giving
them away for free?

00:17:52.938 --> 00:17:54.608
What do you think about that?

00:17:54.639 --> 00:17:58.409
Well, sounds pretty suspicious.

00:17:59.909 --> 00:18:02.909
Remember that wreath dad
brought home that one year?

00:18:04.409 --> 00:18:07.038
Do you mean the one he stole
from, like, a liquor store?

00:18:07.079 --> 00:18:10.478
Yeah, it was a bunch
of empty beer cans.

00:18:10.509 --> 00:18:12.038
That thing was great.

00:18:12.079 --> 00:18:14.208
I bet if i looked
around hard enough,

00:18:14.239 --> 00:18:16.838
I could probably
find one just like it.

00:18:16.878 --> 00:18:18.208
All right...

00:18:18.239 --> 00:18:20.079
Dude...

00:18:20.108 --> 00:18:22.179
What's going on with you? What?

00:18:22.208 --> 00:18:24.679
I mean, since when are you
bing crosby all of a sudden?

00:18:24.708 --> 00:18:26.878
Why do you want to
do christmas so bad?

00:18:26.909 --> 00:18:28.679
Why are you so against it?

00:18:28.708 --> 00:18:30.478
Were your childhood
memories that traumatic?

00:18:30.509 --> 00:18:31.978
No, that has nothing to do with it.

00:18:32.009 --> 00:18:33.809
Then what?

00:18:33.838 --> 00:18:35.639
I mean, i-I just
- I don't get it.

00:18:35.679 --> 00:18:37.838
You haven't talked
about christmas in years.

00:18:40.978 --> 00:18:42.338
Well, yeah.

00:18:43.838 --> 00:18:45.278
This is my last year.

00:18:52.338 --> 00:18:53.478
I know.

00:18:55.909 --> 00:18:57.978
That's why i can't.

00:18:59.639 --> 00:19:01.179
What do you mean?

00:19:04.608 --> 00:19:08.409
I mean i can't just sit around,

00:19:08.438 --> 00:19:11.639
Drinking eggnog,
pretending everything's okay

00:19:11.679 --> 00:19:14.378
When i know next
christmas you'll be dead.

00:19:19.239 --> 00:19:20.639
I just can't.

00:19:35.608 --> 00:19:37.108
Thought you went out.

00:19:37.139 --> 00:19:40.478
Yeah. To get you dinner.

00:19:40.509 --> 00:19:43.739
Don't forget your vegetables.

00:19:53.179 --> 00:19:55.038
I know why you keep a
gun under your pillow.

00:19:58.978 --> 00:20:01.909
No, you don't. Stay
out of my stuff.

00:20:01.938 --> 00:20:04.639
And i know why we lay
salt down everywhere we go.

00:20:04.679 --> 00:20:07.038
No, you don't. Shut up.

00:20:13.509 --> 00:20:16.239
Where'd you get that? That's dad's!

00:20:16.278 --> 00:20:18.478
He's gonna kick your
ass for reading that.

00:20:18.509 --> 00:20:19.938
Are monsters real?

00:20:19.978 --> 00:20:21.938
What?You're crazy.

00:20:21.978 --> 00:20:22.938
Tell me.

00:20:33.838 --> 00:20:37.878
I swear, if you ever tell
dad i told you any of this,

00:20:37.909 --> 00:20:39.438
I will end you.

00:20:39.478 --> 00:20:41.079
Promise.

00:20:47.378 --> 00:20:50.878
Well, the first
thing you have to know

00:20:50.909 --> 00:20:53.878
Is we have the coolest
dad in the world.

00:20:53.909 --> 00:20:55.608
He's a superhero.

00:20:55.639 --> 00:20:57.878
He is? Yeah.

00:20:57.909 --> 00:21:00.438
Monsters are real.

00:21:01.809 --> 00:21:03.708
Dad fights them.

00:21:03.739 --> 00:21:05.509
He's fighting them right now.

00:21:05.538 --> 00:21:08.438
But dad said the monsters
under my bed weren't real.

00:21:08.478 --> 00:21:11.739
That's 'cause he had
already checked under there.

00:21:13.509 --> 00:21:15.278
But, yeah, they're real.

00:21:16.538 --> 00:21:17.878
Almost everything's real.

00:21:17.909 --> 00:21:19.478
Is santa real?

00:21:19.509 --> 00:21:21.778
No.

00:21:25.208 --> 00:21:28.239
If monsters are real,
then they could get us.

00:21:28.278 --> 00:21:30.978
They could get me. Dad's
not gonna let them get you.

00:21:31.009 --> 00:21:32.309
But what if they get him?

00:21:32.338 --> 00:21:34.739
They aren't gonna get dad.

00:21:34.778 --> 00:21:36.679
Dad's, like, the best.

00:21:38.378 --> 00:21:40.778
I read in dad's book
that they got mom.

00:21:44.579 --> 00:21:46.239
It's complicated, sam.

00:21:46.278 --> 00:21:48.079
If they got mom, they can get dad.

00:21:48.108 --> 00:21:50.409
And if they get
dad, they can get us.

00:21:50.438 --> 00:21:52.509
It's not like that.

00:21:54.139 --> 00:21:56.239
Okay, dad's fine.

00:21:56.278 --> 00:21:57.978
We're fine.

00:21:58.009 --> 00:21:59.509
Trust me.

00:22:05.978 --> 00:22:07.179
You okay?

00:22:07.208 --> 00:22:09.509
Yeah.

00:22:12.278 --> 00:22:16.038
Hey, dad's gonna be
here for christmas...

00:22:16.079 --> 00:22:17.679
Just like he always is.

00:22:20.878 --> 00:22:23.208
I just want to go to sleep, okay?

00:22:27.509 --> 00:22:30.239
Yeah, okay.

00:22:34.579 --> 00:22:36.679
It'll all be better
when you wake up.

00:22:39.909 --> 00:22:41.838
You'll see.

00:22:45.579 --> 00:22:47.909
Promise.

00:23:01.938 --> 00:23:04.509
This is where mrs.
Wreath lives, huh?

00:23:04.538 --> 00:23:09.009
Can't you just feel
the evil pagan vibe?

00:23:15.608 --> 00:23:17.409
Yes?

00:23:17.438 --> 00:23:20.239
Please tell me you're the madge carrigan
who makes the meadowsweet wreaths.

00:23:20.278 --> 00:23:21.809
Why, yes, i am.

00:23:21.838 --> 00:23:22.938
Ha! Bingo.

00:23:22.978 --> 00:23:24.878
Well, we were just
admiring your wreaths

00:23:24.909 --> 00:23:27.579
In mr. Sylar's place the other day.

00:23:27.608 --> 00:23:28.809
You were?

00:23:28.838 --> 00:23:30.478
Well, isn't that meadowsweet

00:23:30.509 --> 00:23:32.438
Just the finest-Smelling
thing you ever smelled?

00:23:32.478 --> 00:23:33.778
It sure is.

00:23:33.809 --> 00:23:36.239
But the problem is, is all
your wreaths had sold out

00:23:36.278 --> 00:23:39.038
Before we got the chance
to buy one. Oh, fudge!

00:23:39.079 --> 00:23:41.409
You wouldn't have another one
that we could buy from you?

00:23:41.438 --> 00:23:44.739
No, i'm afraid those were the
only ones i had for this season.

00:23:44.778 --> 00:23:46.108
Tell me something -

00:23:46.139 --> 00:23:48.538
Why did you decide to make
them out of meadowsweet?

00:23:48.579 --> 00:23:50.608
Why, the smell, of course!

00:23:50.639 --> 00:23:52.878
I don't think i've ever
smelled anything finer.

00:23:52.909 --> 00:23:54.579
Yeah, um, you mentioned that.

00:23:54.608 --> 00:23:56.278
What's going on, honey?

00:23:56.309 --> 00:23:59.579
Well, just some nice boys
asking about my wreaths, dear.

00:23:59.608 --> 00:24:01.778
Oh, the wreaths are
fine. Fine wreaths.

00:24:01.809 --> 00:24:04.978
Oh, care for some peanut brittle?

00:24:06.338 --> 00:24:08.409
We're okay.

00:24:13.538 --> 00:24:14.608
I knew it!

00:24:14.639 --> 00:24:16.778
Something was way
off with those two.

00:24:16.809 --> 00:24:17.909
What'd you find?

00:24:17.938 --> 00:24:19.309
The carrigans lived
in seattle last year,

00:24:19.338 --> 00:24:21.108
Where two abductions took
place right around christmas.

00:24:21.139 --> 00:24:22.978
They moved here in january.

00:24:23.009 --> 00:24:25.639
All that christmas crap in their
house wasn't boughs of holly.

00:24:25.679 --> 00:24:27.139
It was vervain and mint.

00:24:27.179 --> 00:24:29.378
Pagan stuff? Serious pagan stuff.

00:24:29.409 --> 00:24:31.538
So, what, ozzie and harriet
are keeping a pagan god

00:24:31.579 --> 00:24:33.978
Hidden underneath their
plastic-Covered couch?

00:24:34.009 --> 00:24:35.509
I don't know. We got
to check them out.

00:24:35.538 --> 00:24:37.009
So, what about bobby?

00:24:37.038 --> 00:24:40.009
He's sure evergreen stakes
will kill this thing, right?

00:24:40.038 --> 00:24:42.438
Yeah, he's sure.

00:25:08.038 --> 00:25:10.139
See? Plastic.

00:25:47.478 --> 00:25:49.309
Hey, dean.

00:27:17.838 --> 00:27:19.108
Sam!

00:27:32.509 --> 00:27:35.909
Gosh, i wish you boys
hadn't come down here.

00:27:55.139 --> 00:27:57.438
Dean?

00:27:57.478 --> 00:27:59.809
You okay?

00:27:59.838 --> 00:28:01.538
Yeah, i think so.

00:28:02.978 --> 00:28:06.809
So, i guess we're dealing
with mr. And mrs. God.

00:28:06.838 --> 00:28:08.878
Nice to know.

00:28:08.909 --> 00:28:11.878
Ooh, and here we
thought you two lazybones

00:28:11.909 --> 00:28:15.038
Were gonna sleep straight
through all the fun stuff.

00:28:15.079 --> 00:28:17.478
Miss all this? Nah, we're partyers.

00:28:17.509 --> 00:28:19.309
Isn't he a kick in
the pants, honey?

00:28:19.338 --> 00:28:21.538
You're hunters is what you are.

00:28:21.579 --> 00:28:23.038
And you're pagan gods.

00:28:23.079 --> 00:28:25.809
So, why don't we just call it
even and go our separate ways?

00:28:25.838 --> 00:28:27.538
So you can bring more
hunters and kill us?

00:28:27.579 --> 00:28:29.478
I don't think so!

00:28:29.509 --> 00:28:31.708
You should have thought about
that before snacking on humans.

00:28:31.739 --> 00:28:33.438
Oh, now, don't get all wet.

00:28:33.478 --> 00:28:37.938
Oh, why, we used to take over
a hundred tributes a year.

00:28:37.978 --> 00:28:40.438
And that's a fact.

00:28:40.478 --> 00:28:43.538
Now what do we take?
What, two? Three?

00:28:44.579 --> 00:28:46.538
Hardy boys here make five.

00:28:48.409 --> 00:28:50.409
Now, that's not so bad, is it?

00:28:50.438 --> 00:28:52.909
You say it like that, you
guys are the cunninghams.

00:28:52.938 --> 00:28:55.038
You, mister, better
show us a little respect.

00:28:55.079 --> 00:28:57.909
Or what? You'll eat us?

00:28:57.938 --> 00:28:58.938
Not so fast.

00:28:58.978 --> 00:29:01.579
There's rituals to
be followed first.

00:29:01.608 --> 00:29:03.838
Oh, we're just
sticklers for ritual.

00:29:03.878 --> 00:29:05.838
And you know what kicks
off the whole shebang?

00:29:05.878 --> 00:29:07.739
Let me guess -Meadowsweet.

00:29:07.778 --> 00:29:09.909
Oh, shucks -You're
all out of wreaths.

00:29:09.938 --> 00:29:12.239
I guess we'll just have to
cancel the sacrifice, huh?

00:29:12.278 --> 00:29:15.409
Oh, don't be such a gloomy gus.

00:29:15.438 --> 00:29:17.409
There.

00:29:19.909 --> 00:29:22.309
Don't they just look darling?

00:29:22.338 --> 00:29:23.838
Good enough to eat.

00:29:25.139 --> 00:29:28.378
All righty-Roo. Step number two.

00:29:33.778 --> 00:29:34.809
Sammy.

00:29:34.838 --> 00:29:35.639
Sammy!

00:29:35.679 --> 00:29:37.938
D
- Don't!

00:29:37.978 --> 00:29:40.079
Leave him alone,
you son of a bitch!

00:29:40.108 --> 00:29:43.478
Hear how they talk to us? To gods?

00:29:43.509 --> 00:29:46.639
Listen, pal, back in the day,
we were worshiped by millions.

00:29:46.679 --> 00:29:49.108
Times have changed!
Tell me about it.

00:29:49.139 --> 00:29:52.009
All of a sudden, this jesus character
is the hot new thing in town.

00:29:52.038 --> 00:29:54.309
All of a sudden, our altars
are being burned down,

00:29:54.338 --> 00:29:56.579
And we're being hunted
down like common monsters.

00:29:56.608 --> 00:30:01.079
But did we say a peep?
Oh, no, no, no, we did not.

00:30:01.108 --> 00:30:03.108
Two millennium.

00:30:03.139 --> 00:30:07.139
We kept a low profile.
We got jobs, a mortgage.

00:30:07.179 --> 00:30:08.739
We -What was that word, dear?

00:30:08.778 --> 00:30:10.139
We assimilated.

00:30:10.179 --> 00:30:12.208
Yeah, we assimilated.

00:30:12.239 --> 00:30:14.878
Why, we play bridge on
tuesdays and fridays.

00:30:14.909 --> 00:30:16.639
We're just like everybody else.

00:30:16.679 --> 00:30:18.778
You're not blending in as
smooth as you think, lady.

00:30:18.809 --> 00:30:21.878
This might pinch a bit, dear.

00:30:21.909 --> 00:30:23.708
You bitch!

00:30:23.739 --> 00:30:25.409
Oh, my goodness me!

00:30:25.438 --> 00:30:27.938
Somebody owes a nickel
to the swear jar.

00:30:27.978 --> 00:30:30.838
Oh, do you know what i say
when i feel like swearing?

00:30:30.878 --> 00:30:32.478
"Fudge. "

00:30:32.509 --> 00:30:34.708
I'll try and remember that!

00:30:34.739 --> 00:30:36.708
You boys have no idea
how lucky you are.

00:30:36.739 --> 00:30:39.409
There was a time when
kids came from miles around

00:30:39.438 --> 00:30:41.278
Just to be sitting where you are.

00:30:41.309 --> 00:30:44.378
What do you think
you're doing with those?

00:30:44.409 --> 00:30:47.179
You fudging touch me again,
i'll fudging kill you!

00:30:47.208 --> 00:30:48.679
Very good.

00:30:56.778 --> 00:30:58.838
No, don't.

00:31:07.038 --> 00:31:09.938
Oh, we've got a winner!

00:31:23.739 --> 00:31:24.838
What else, dear?

00:31:24.878 --> 00:31:28.338
Well, let's see. Uh,
fingernail, blood...

00:31:30.708 --> 00:31:32.179
I forgot the tooth!

00:31:32.208 --> 00:31:34.438
Oh, dear!

00:31:34.478 --> 00:31:36.338
Merry christmas, sam.

00:31:42.438 --> 00:31:45.509
Open wide... and say, "ahh. "

00:31:49.608 --> 00:31:52.208
Somebody gonna get that?

00:31:54.038 --> 00:31:55.739
You should get that.

00:31:58.639 --> 00:32:00.338
Come on.

00:32:03.309 --> 00:32:05.438
Merry christmas!

00:32:05.478 --> 00:32:07.338
I told you i smelled fruitcake.

00:32:07.378 --> 00:32:08.909
You shouldn't have.

00:32:08.938 --> 00:32:10.478
Oh, bite your tongue.
It's my pleasure.

00:32:10.509 --> 00:32:11.739
It looks scrumptious!

00:32:11.778 --> 00:32:13.878
Neal and i are going
caroling. You care to join?

00:32:13.909 --> 00:32:15.108
You know, we would...

00:32:15.139 --> 00:32:18.079
It's my back
- Darn thing's giving me fits.

00:32:18.108 --> 00:32:19.739
Oh, well, that's a shame.

00:32:19.778 --> 00:32:21.909
- Oh, well. Merry christmas.
- And to you, too, dear.

00:32:21.938 --> 00:32:24.878
- Hey, are we still on for bridge tomorrow?
- With bells on!

00:32:24.909 --> 00:32:27.009
- Yes! Okay,
bye. -Bye-Bye.

00:32:35.639 --> 00:32:37.778
Now, where were we?

00:32:51.708 --> 00:32:53.608
What do we do now?!

00:32:53.639 --> 00:32:55.909
The evergreen stake's
in the basement!

00:32:55.938 --> 00:32:57.938
Well, we need more evergreen, dean!

00:32:59.338 --> 00:33:01.608
I think i just found us some more.

00:33:01.639 --> 00:33:04.378
Help me get this.

00:33:04.409 --> 00:33:05.438
Go!

00:33:07.309 --> 00:33:09.579
Come on!

00:33:36.038 --> 00:33:38.509
You little thing...

00:33:39.608 --> 00:33:41.509
I loved that tree.

00:33:52.179 --> 00:33:54.079
Madge!

00:34:24.838 --> 00:34:27.079
Merry christmas.

00:34:43.909 --> 00:34:45.679
Sam, wake up.

00:34:48.378 --> 00:34:50.679
Dad was here. Look what he brought.

00:34:50.709 --> 00:34:52.739
Dad was here?

00:34:52.778 --> 00:34:55.709
Yeah. Look at this.
We made a killing.

00:34:55.739 --> 00:34:58.878
Why didn't he try to wake me up?

00:34:58.909 --> 00:35:02.179
He tried to, like a thousand times.

00:35:02.209 --> 00:35:04.278
He did?

00:35:04.309 --> 00:35:08.009
Yeah. Did i tell you he would
give us christmas or what?

00:35:09.378 --> 00:35:10.539
Go on, dive in.

00:35:24.739 --> 00:35:27.009
What is it?

00:35:27.039 --> 00:35:29.079
Sapphire barbie?

00:35:29.108 --> 00:35:32.278
Dad probably thinks you're a girl.

00:35:32.309 --> 00:35:33.338
Shut up.

00:35:33.378 --> 00:35:34.809
Open that one.

00:35:43.709 --> 00:35:45.309
Dad never showed, did he?

00:35:45.338 --> 00:35:47.039
Yeah, he did, i swear.

00:35:47.079 --> 00:35:50.108
Dean... where'd you
get all this stuff?

00:35:55.079 --> 00:35:56.979
Nice house up the block.

00:35:59.239 --> 00:36:02.209
I swear i didn't know
they were chick presents.

00:36:04.739 --> 00:36:07.639
Look, i'm sure dad would
have been here if he could.

00:36:07.679 --> 00:36:09.479
If he's alive.

00:36:09.509 --> 00:36:10.639
Don't say that.

00:36:10.679 --> 00:36:12.179
Of course he's alive.

00:36:12.209 --> 00:36:13.878
He's dad.

00:36:22.539 --> 00:36:24.838
Here. Take this.

00:36:24.878 --> 00:36:27.309
No. No, that's for dad.

00:36:27.338 --> 00:36:30.179
Dad lied to me.

00:36:30.209 --> 00:36:32.009
I want you to have it.

00:36:35.439 --> 00:36:37.838
- You sure?
- I'm sure.

00:36:55.539 --> 00:36:58.809
Thank you, sam. I-I love it.

00:37:17.679 --> 00:37:20.179
Hey. You get the beer?

00:37:20.209 --> 00:37:22.179
What's all this?

00:37:22.209 --> 00:37:25.209
What do you think it is? It's
- It's christmas.

00:37:30.778 --> 00:37:32.878
What made you change your mind?

00:37:35.409 --> 00:37:37.409
Here, uh...

00:37:37.439 --> 00:37:39.939
Try the eggnog.

00:37:39.979 --> 00:37:42.739
Let me know if it
needs some more kick.

00:37:47.709 --> 00:37:49.039
No, we're good.

00:37:49.079 --> 00:37:50.209
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:37:50.239 --> 00:37:53.378
Good. Well, uh, have a seat.

00:37:53.409 --> 00:37:56.108
Let's do christmas
stuff or whatever.

00:37:56.139 --> 00:37:58.009
All right, first thing's first.

00:38:06.979 --> 00:38:08.509
Merry christmas, sam.

00:38:10.639 --> 00:38:13.278
- Where'd you get these?
- Someplace special.

00:38:14.378 --> 00:38:16.108
The gas mart down the street.

00:38:16.139 --> 00:38:17.778
Open them up.

00:38:17.809 --> 00:38:20.939
Well, great minds
think alike, dean.

00:38:20.979 --> 00:38:22.939
Really?

00:38:22.979 --> 00:38:24.639
There you go.

